1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,800
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:41,600
[bleating]

3
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:49,950
[GIRL] My lady, where are you?

4
00:01:51,410 --> 00:01:53,200
My lady!

5
00:01:54,780 --> 00:01:55,950
[sighs]

6
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:58,580
Goodness,
what are you doing out here?

7
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:01,080
It's time for you
to get ready to leave.

8
00:02:02,710 --> 00:02:03,960
[TÖREGENE]
Be right there.

9
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:10,470
[wind blows]

10
00:02:11,970 --> 00:02:14,680
[TÖREGENE]
Farewell, Naiman.

11
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,010
♪

12
00:02:17,510 --> 00:02:20,020
[TÖREGENE] As someone born
into the Naimans

13
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,850
whose nation lay far
to the west of here,

14
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:26,520
it was arranged that I would
marry into the Merkits,

15
00:02:26,650 --> 00:02:28,650
with whom we shared an alliance.

16
00:02:29,110 --> 00:02:30,610
[GIRL] I wonder about
the Merkit tribes

17
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:31,900
and what their lives are like.

18
00:02:32,070 --> 00:02:33,030
[TÖREGENE'S SISTER-IN-LAW]
They live in the woods

19
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:34,160
just to the north.

20
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:36,530
Many of them are skilled bowmen
called Mergen.

21
00:02:36,660 --> 00:02:38,080
Mergen?

22
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:40,080
They're known
as the Mergen people,

23
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:41,580
hence the name "Merkits."

24
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:44,830
[TÖREGENE] In other words,
barbaric hunters.

25
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:45,960
[Töregene's sister-in-law
sniffles]

26
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:48,090
[TÖREGENE]
Well, it matters not.

27
00:02:48,210 --> 00:02:50,050
I am nothing
but a valuable gift.

28
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:53,260
No different
from a precious gemstone

29
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:54,970
or a fine fur pelt.

30
00:02:55,930 --> 00:02:57,640
But that's all well.

31
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:01,680
I'm fulfilling my role,
and accept it with pride.

32
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:12,650
[senior wife chuckles]

33
00:03:13,070 --> 00:03:15,450
[TÖREGENE] So this is where
the Merkits live.

34
00:03:15,570 --> 00:03:18,160
It's much drearier
than I expected.

35
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,330
[indistinct chatter]

36
00:03:19,450 --> 00:03:21,290
[TÖREGENE]
Why are there so few men?

37
00:03:21,410 --> 00:03:22,910
-[DAYIR] Töregene.
-Uh?

38
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:24,540
Glad you're safe.

39
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:27,790
I am sorry, I know this isn't
much of a welcome.

40
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:31,170
Are you startled to learn
your husband's such an old man?

41
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:32,510
No.

42
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:36,220
Well, so be it.

43
00:03:36,630 --> 00:03:40,140
Marrying a much older man
is far from rare.

44
00:03:41,810 --> 00:03:45,020
And yet,
after our wedding ceremony,

45
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:47,560
Dayir never made any advances.

46
00:03:50,190 --> 00:03:52,360
On the contrary...

47
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:54,240
So, you'll be going away again?

48
00:03:54,360 --> 00:03:57,320
Please forgive me
for always leaving you behind.

49
00:03:57,950 --> 00:03:59,700
And why do we keep moving camps?

50
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,660
It seems like
we just arrived here.

51
00:04:02,790 --> 00:04:03,750
[Dayir sighs]

52
00:04:04,040 --> 00:04:06,790
We can't stay
in one place for too long.

53
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:09,330
-You had best get going now.
-[gasps]

54
00:04:09,670 --> 00:04:11,000
[DAYIR] Chuu!

55
00:04:14,510 --> 00:04:17,880
-If you need anything, I'm here.
-Thank you.

56
00:04:18,010 --> 00:04:19,680
-I, uh--
-[GIRL] Mistress...

57
00:04:19,800 --> 00:04:21,760
What should I do with this?

58
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:23,770
Oh, well, let's see now.

59
00:04:24,930 --> 00:04:26,480
[TÖREGENE]
Do all of the other tribes

60
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:28,940
keep moving their camps
as often as we do?

61
00:04:29,060 --> 00:04:30,810
-Right over there. Please.
-[TÖREGENE] No.

62
00:04:30,940 --> 00:04:33,480
There's something strange
going on here.

63
00:04:33,610 --> 00:04:36,650
It feels as if we're fleeing
from something.

64
00:04:39,120 --> 00:04:42,830
Well, I suppose
there's no use in worrying.

65
00:04:43,370 --> 00:04:46,200
I'm only here to be a gemstone.

66
00:04:46,330 --> 00:04:49,880
And what good would it do
for a gemstone to be concerned?

67
00:04:51,830 --> 00:04:52,920
[breathes uneasily]

68
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,550
I want to go back to Naiman.

69
00:04:58,380 --> 00:05:00,220
[birds chirping]

70
00:05:01,850 --> 00:05:04,430
-[bird screeching]
-[Töregene pants]

71
00:05:05,850 --> 00:05:07,890
They won't notice
if I go missing.

72
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,690
I know Chieftain Dayir won't.

73
00:05:10,810 --> 00:05:13,480
Nor will anybody else
who's in the tribe.

74
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:15,650
-[GIRL] Hold on!
-[Töregene gasps]

75
00:05:17,280 --> 00:05:18,900
Stay right where you are!

76
00:05:19,530 --> 00:05:20,660
[gasps]

77
00:05:24,990 --> 00:05:26,250
[panting]

78
00:05:26,370 --> 00:05:27,750
That was close, wasn't it?

79
00:05:28,120 --> 00:05:29,620
Are you all right?

80
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:35,050
You truly live up
to your title of Mergen.

81
00:05:35,170 --> 00:05:37,380
Ah, not really. Easy shot.

82
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:38,630
Huh? Oh my...

83
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:41,010
You must be Töregene,
aren't you?

84
00:05:41,130 --> 00:05:43,470
Then that means
you're my new mother.

85
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:45,890
[TÖREGENE] Huh?

86
00:05:46,310 --> 00:05:47,890
My name is Khulan.

87
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:49,100
I'm Dayir's daughter.

88
00:05:49,230 --> 00:05:50,350
Qultuqan...

89
00:05:50,810 --> 00:05:52,190
Is my name.

90
00:05:53,020 --> 00:05:54,770
-[chuckles softly]
-[Khulan laughs]

91
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,900
[TÖREGENE]
Khulan was Dayir's child.

92
00:05:57,020 --> 00:05:59,690
And Qultuqan was the child
of another chieftain.

93
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:02,320
[KHULAN] See that? If you start
going down this river,

94
00:06:02,450 --> 00:06:04,870
it splits off into the Qara
and Dal rivers.

95
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:06,990
Further down,
both of them wind around

96
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:09,290
until they feed
into the Selenge River.

97
00:06:09,410 --> 00:06:12,080
And that's the place where
Qultuqan and I were born.

98
00:06:12,210 --> 00:06:13,370
You were?

99
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:15,670
If you go all the way
down the rivers,

100
00:06:15,790 --> 00:06:18,210
do you know where every single
one of them ends up?

101
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,670
[TÖREGENE] Hmm...

102
00:06:19,800 --> 00:06:20,670
[Khulan grunts]

103
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:22,550
So you know
the star to the north

104
00:06:22,680 --> 00:06:23,970
that doesn't move at all?

105
00:06:24,090 --> 00:06:25,010
♪

106
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:26,260
[KHULAN] Right underneath it,

107
00:06:26,390 --> 00:06:28,390
there's the biggest hole
you can imagine.

108
00:06:28,510 --> 00:06:29,680
And that's the place

109
00:06:29,930 --> 00:06:32,600
where the rivers from
all over the entire world flow.

110
00:06:32,730 --> 00:06:35,730
Wow. I've never heard
that before.

111
00:06:35,860 --> 00:06:37,230
[Khulan chuckles]

112
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:39,740
Well, it's not like
you've seen it for yourself.

113
00:06:40,240 --> 00:06:42,070
Come on. Cut it out.

114
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:43,360
Is that true?

115
00:06:43,490 --> 00:06:45,570
Neither of us
has the power like a kam

116
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:46,870
to communicate with spirits.

117
00:06:46,990 --> 00:06:48,620
My father is a kam, though.

118
00:06:48,990 --> 00:06:50,040
And he has been out

119
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:52,080
where the rivers
end a lot of times!

120
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:55,880
His soul turns into a bird,
and he flies way up there.

121
00:06:56,210 --> 00:06:57,340
A kam?

122
00:06:57,460 --> 00:07:00,210
Hmm. I wish
I could do things like that

123
00:07:00,340 --> 00:07:02,010
and have kam powers, too.

124
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:04,590
Or be somebody who has
great skills with a bow.

125
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:06,390
You are a pretty terrible shot.

126
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:08,390
Enough! Hold your tongue!

127
00:07:08,510 --> 00:07:10,140
You said it yourself, Khulan!

128
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:12,100
-[KHULAN] I'm serious.
-[QULTUQAN] So am I.

129
00:07:12,230 --> 00:07:13,690
[Töregene laughs]

130
00:07:13,810 --> 00:07:15,940
It looks like
we got you laughing.

131
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:17,900
[TÖREGENE]
Oh, pardon me. [laughs]

132
00:07:18,020 --> 00:07:20,150
[Khulan laughs]

133
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:21,650
[Qultuqan laughs]

134
00:07:21,780 --> 00:07:22,990
♪

135
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:24,860
[TÖREGENE] On that day,

136
00:07:24,950 --> 00:07:27,780
it seemed like something
deep inside had changed.

137
00:07:27,910 --> 00:07:29,030
♪

138
00:07:29,790 --> 00:07:32,370
It felt as though
the very world around me

139
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:35,670
stirred my soul
in so many different ways.

140
00:07:45,880 --> 00:07:49,470
I experienced
true laughter and joy.

141
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:03,690
Discontent and a sense
of sorrow too.

142
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:04,990
♪

143
00:08:16,290 --> 00:08:18,250
As the days passed by,

144
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:20,840
I came to love
every moment here.

145
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:32,890
And then for the first time,

146
00:08:33,470 --> 00:08:34,930
I understood.

147
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:42,900
Wake up, everyone!

148
00:08:43,690 --> 00:08:45,190
We must flee.

149
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:46,360
What happened?

150
00:08:46,490 --> 00:08:47,950
Our chieftains' armies
have been bested!

151
00:08:48,070 --> 00:08:50,530
-[all gasp]
-The enemy will be here soon!

152
00:08:51,070 --> 00:08:52,620
-[horse neighs]
-[grunts]

153
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:55,750
[soldiers yelling distantly]

154
00:08:55,870 --> 00:08:58,290
[screaming]

155
00:08:58,410 --> 00:08:59,790
Into the woods!

156
00:09:00,080 --> 00:09:01,580
[panting]

157
00:09:01,710 --> 00:09:04,630
[QULTUQAN]
Khulan, Töregene, come this way.

158
00:09:04,750 --> 00:09:05,800
[KHULAN] Qultuqan!

159
00:09:08,920 --> 00:09:10,550
[people crying]

160
00:09:10,680 --> 00:09:12,050
[QULTUQAN'S BROTHER]
How much did they plunder?

161
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:14,350
[QULTUQAN]
Qudu's family is gone,

162
00:09:14,470 --> 00:09:16,350
as are Chilaun's wife
and children.

163
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:18,810
[DAYIR] Töregene!

164
00:09:19,140 --> 00:09:20,560
[KHULAN] Father, you're here.

165
00:09:20,690 --> 00:09:22,810
[DAYIR]
You must have been scared.

166
00:09:22,940 --> 00:09:25,320
I want to thank you
for protecting our Khulan.

167
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:26,360
Mm-mm.

168
00:09:26,490 --> 00:09:28,610
She was the one
who protected me.

169
00:09:28,740 --> 00:09:31,160
What on earth is going on here?

170
00:09:31,570 --> 00:09:33,910
So, the Naimans never told you
of the danger

171
00:09:34,030 --> 00:09:35,410
we have been facing?

172
00:09:35,990 --> 00:09:38,330
Well, I suppose
I cannot blame them.

173
00:09:39,750 --> 00:09:41,750
Our people have a true enemy.

174
00:09:41,880 --> 00:09:44,000
Temüjin of the Mongols.

175
00:09:45,710 --> 00:09:50,170
The vicious man who now bears
the title of Genghis Khan.

176
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:54,890
Genghis Khan?

177
00:09:55,010 --> 00:09:56,850
[DAYIR]
As long as I can remember,

178
00:09:56,970 --> 00:10:00,350
we Merkits have engaged
in skirmishes with the Mongols.

179
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,560
They have taken many
of our families

180
00:10:02,690 --> 00:10:04,810
and deprived us
of our possessions.

181
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:07,150
Yet we always
struck back in kind.

182
00:10:08,360 --> 00:10:11,780
But with Temüjin
as their leader, it all changed.

183
00:10:11,900 --> 00:10:14,660
And the very balance
of the steppe was lost.

184
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:16,740
The reason you were
given away

185
00:10:16,870 --> 00:10:18,660
to become the wife of an old man

186
00:10:18,790 --> 00:10:22,160
was to strengthen our alliance
against the Mongols.

187
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:27,210
That said, it seems the end
may finally be near.

188
00:10:27,880 --> 00:10:30,970
Say, brother,
if the Mongols do win,

189
00:10:31,090 --> 00:10:32,470
what will become of us then?

190
00:10:32,590 --> 00:10:33,880
You have to ask?

191
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:35,220
They'll slaughter the men

192
00:10:35,350 --> 00:10:37,310
and take all our women
and children.

193
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:41,230
[QULTUQAN] I'm really afraid.
I don't want to die.

194
00:10:41,770 --> 00:10:44,770
[QULTUQAN'S BROTHER] Fool!
You call yourself a Merkit man?

195
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:45,980
[Dayir sighs]

196
00:10:53,650 --> 00:10:54,780
[MAN] Usun.

197
00:10:54,910 --> 00:10:56,240
Usun.

198
00:10:56,780 --> 00:10:59,240
Usun. Means "flowing river."

199
00:10:59,620 --> 00:11:01,080
For his role as our kam,

200
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:03,580
the earth bestowed
that title upon him.

201
00:11:03,910 --> 00:11:05,040
Listen well.

202
00:11:05,210 --> 00:11:07,920
No one is to utter
a word until I've finished.

203
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:13,050
For I shall beseech
the spirits to guide me.

204
00:11:14,630 --> 00:11:16,350
[wind blows]

205
00:11:17,970 --> 00:11:19,350
[DAYIR] Oh, spirits,

206
00:11:19,470 --> 00:11:21,480
lift me up to the heavens.

207
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:24,480
Show me what lies in our future.

208
00:11:24,770 --> 00:11:26,270
[inhales deeply]

209
00:11:26,400 --> 00:11:28,060
[♪ drum beating]

210
00:11:28,570 --> 00:11:29,860
[breathing heavily]

211
00:11:42,950 --> 00:11:44,370
[wind blowing]

212
00:12:10,150 --> 00:12:11,940
[exclaims]

213
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:16,400
♪

214
00:12:21,120 --> 00:12:22,200
[gasps]

215
00:12:27,420 --> 00:12:30,250
[Dayir exclaims]

216
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:31,500
♪

217
00:12:44,270 --> 00:12:45,600
[Dayir groans]

218
00:12:45,730 --> 00:12:46,770
Usun.

219
00:12:46,890 --> 00:12:48,230
[Dayir pants]

220
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:51,980
Khulan, are you there?

221
00:12:52,110 --> 00:12:53,230
[Khulan gasps]

222
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,070
Yes, I'm right here, Father.

223
00:12:56,780 --> 00:12:59,030
I could see a very lush steppe.

224
00:12:59,280 --> 00:13:02,780
A river branching
and feeding into many others.

225
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:05,870
And when I followed the river
to its source,

226
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:09,210
atop a mountain that was
as tall as the heavens,

227
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:11,380
I found a pure riverhead.

228
00:13:11,920 --> 00:13:14,380
All those rivers
were bloodlines.

229
00:13:14,500 --> 00:13:16,880
And they signified
that Mongol progeny

230
00:13:17,010 --> 00:13:19,470
will soon be spreading across
this great land.

231
00:13:19,590 --> 00:13:20,640
So...

232
00:13:20,760 --> 00:13:23,220
We are destined to lose
to the Mongols.

233
00:13:23,350 --> 00:13:24,510
[all exclaim]

234
00:13:25,770 --> 00:13:27,140
Then does that mean

235
00:13:27,270 --> 00:13:29,440
each one of us
is going to be killed?

236
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:31,940
No. I won't allow that
to happen.

237
00:13:32,060 --> 00:13:33,150
[Khulan gasps]

238
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,610
[DAYIR]
According to the spirits,

239
00:13:34,730 --> 00:13:36,230
the Merkit blood will live on

240
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:38,240
even after we've
surrendered to them.

241
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:41,620
Do you really think Genghis Khan
will show us any mercy?

242
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:44,160
Yes, but we'll have to give
appropriate tribute

243
00:13:44,280 --> 00:13:46,240
in exchange
for such a thing, of course.

244
00:13:46,370 --> 00:13:47,290
[all sigh]

245
00:13:47,830 --> 00:13:51,460
[DAYIR] A pure riverhead
to appease Genghis Khan.

246
00:13:51,580 --> 00:13:53,960
-I shall offer my daughter.
-[all gasp]

247
00:13:54,090 --> 00:13:55,290
Khulan.

248
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:57,840
[grunts] You mustn't!

249
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,010
I won't allow you
to sacrifice her.

250
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:03,180
She's a human
with her own mind and will!

251
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,890
Not a gemstone or a fur pelt!

252
00:14:06,010 --> 00:14:07,140
[whimpers]

253
00:14:08,430 --> 00:14:12,060
She's not... [cries softly]
like me.

254
00:14:14,360 --> 00:14:18,990
Töregene, thank you so much,
but I will be fine.

255
00:14:19,320 --> 00:14:20,700
Khulan?

256
00:14:22,070 --> 00:14:25,330
In all honesty,
I am happy, Father.

257
00:14:25,490 --> 00:14:27,410
I've always resented
being a girl

258
00:14:27,530 --> 00:14:29,410
and needing others' protection.

259
00:14:29,540 --> 00:14:30,710
But this way,

260
00:14:30,830 --> 00:14:31,960
I can serve as the arrow

261
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:33,630
that will keep
each one of you safe.

262
00:14:33,750 --> 00:14:35,210
You mean...

263
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,670
Merkits are masters of the bow.

264
00:14:38,050 --> 00:14:39,800
And as a daughter
of the Mergens,

265
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:42,300
this is my chance
to take down a wolf.

266
00:14:42,760 --> 00:14:44,300
♪

267
00:14:46,930 --> 00:14:49,390
[TÖREGENE]
So we gathered together

268
00:14:49,520 --> 00:14:51,350
and surrendered to the Mongols.

269
00:14:52,350 --> 00:14:55,100
Khulan managed to sever
the chains of hostility

270
00:14:55,230 --> 00:14:58,480
that had bound the Mongols
and Merkits for so long,

271
00:14:59,480 --> 00:15:01,990
saving countless Merkit lives.

272
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:03,530
♪

273
00:15:06,120 --> 00:15:08,580
But Qultuqan
and the other Merkit tribes

274
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:10,200
didn't join the rest of us,

275
00:15:10,330 --> 00:15:12,330
choosing to stand
in bold defiance

276
00:15:12,460 --> 00:15:13,660
until the very end.

277
00:15:13,790 --> 00:15:15,920
Fleeing westward on foot.

278
00:15:16,710 --> 00:15:18,250
♪

279
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:21,380
That should be everybody.

280
00:15:21,510 --> 00:15:23,590
[WOMAN] Why did you summon
all of us here?

281
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:25,260
[TÖREGENE]
There are only young girls.

282
00:15:25,380 --> 00:15:27,300
Are you Dayir Usun?

283
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:29,560
We serve under Prince Ögedei,

284
00:15:29,680 --> 00:15:31,470
the third son of the Khan.

285
00:15:31,930 --> 00:15:33,810
Our role is at the rear
of the army,

286
00:15:33,930 --> 00:15:35,640
keeping watch over the supplies.

287
00:15:35,770 --> 00:15:38,690
Ah, sounds like
I can rest assured then.

288
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:40,690
These girls are
in your hands now.

289
00:15:40,820 --> 00:15:42,530
-[all gasp]
-Chieftain Dayir!

290
00:15:43,450 --> 00:15:45,700
After a long discussion,
we have decided

291
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:47,910
to hand all of you over
to the Mongol nobles.

292
00:15:48,030 --> 00:15:49,240
No! Why?

293
00:15:49,370 --> 00:15:52,620
Come now, my dear.
You must listen carefully.

294
00:15:52,790 --> 00:15:54,910
The Mongols may have
spared us our lives,

295
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:57,000
but that's where
their courtesy ends.

296
00:15:57,120 --> 00:16:00,040
They haven't yet forgiven us
for past confrontations.

297
00:16:00,170 --> 00:16:01,460
-[breathes shakily]
-I've no doubt

298
00:16:01,590 --> 00:16:03,090
we'll soon be reduced to slaves.

299
00:16:03,510 --> 00:16:05,550
But you aren't
like the rest of us.

300
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:08,220
You have your whole lives
ahead of you,

301
00:16:08,340 --> 00:16:11,560
so go on
and find true happiness.

302
00:16:13,010 --> 00:16:14,430
As for you lot...

303
00:16:14,560 --> 00:16:15,560
Just make sure

304
00:16:15,680 --> 00:16:17,480
you tell your prince
and your Khan

305
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,310
that these women
are no longer Merkits

306
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:21,320
from this moment forward, yes?

307
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:22,900
Do you understand me?

308
00:16:23,030 --> 00:16:25,240
[stutters] I'll pass it on.

309
00:16:25,450 --> 00:16:26,570
[SOLDIER] Huh?

310
00:16:27,490 --> 00:16:29,120
-[DAYIR] Töregene.
-Huh?

311
00:16:29,490 --> 00:16:31,080
Open your hand.

312
00:16:36,250 --> 00:16:37,830
This is a Jada stone.

313
00:16:38,210 --> 00:16:40,750
You can bring forth
storms with it.

314
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:43,170
Wish that I had
a better parting gift.

315
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:45,090
It's all I have left.

316
00:16:46,220 --> 00:16:49,470
You've brought me nothing
but joy. I'm grateful.

317
00:16:49,590 --> 00:16:50,890
[Töregene gasps softly]

318
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:52,510
[DAYIR] Farewell.

319
00:16:53,970 --> 00:16:56,020
Live on with a smile.

320
00:17:04,650 --> 00:17:06,280
[TÖREGENE] It was eerily quiet

321
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,360
in the middle
of that fateful night.

322
00:17:10,910 --> 00:17:12,280
[SOLDIER 1] Ready the horses!

323
00:17:12,410 --> 00:17:14,200
-Hurry!
-[SOLDIER 2] Right away!

324
00:17:14,950 --> 00:17:17,410
-[panting]
-[panicked chatter]

325
00:17:19,330 --> 00:17:21,210
[TÖREGENE]
The sky was burning...

326
00:17:21,330 --> 00:17:23,000
Soaked in blood.

327
00:17:23,130 --> 00:17:26,170
An unearthly sight the likes
of which I'd never seen.

328
00:17:26,510 --> 00:17:28,130
[SOLDIER 1]
What's happening out there?

329
00:17:28,260 --> 00:17:29,510
[SOLDIER 2] A rebellion.

330
00:17:29,630 --> 00:17:31,180
The captives have dug in
on the mountain.

331
00:17:31,680 --> 00:17:34,010
Prince Ögedei's army
is about to move out.

332
00:17:34,140 --> 00:17:36,560
-That vile Dayir Usun.
-[whimpers]

333
00:17:36,680 --> 00:17:39,390
You can never take Merkits
at their word.

334
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:40,850
-[TÖREGENE] Move it.
-[grunts]

335
00:17:41,440 --> 00:17:42,770
-Chuu!
-[horse neighs]

336
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:44,570
[SOLDIER] Hey! Wait!

337
00:17:48,240 --> 00:17:49,740
[TÖREGENE]
Even though the Mongols

338
00:17:49,860 --> 00:17:51,410
had shown them
all forgiveness...

339
00:17:54,070 --> 00:17:55,330
deep inside,

340
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:57,830
they had never once forgiven
their oppressors.

341
00:17:58,250 --> 00:18:01,210
[DAYIR] We were raised
as hunters of the forest,

342
00:18:01,330 --> 00:18:03,880
and we won't ever be
a sheep herder's slave.

343
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:06,840
Go on and find true happiness.

344
00:18:07,460 --> 00:18:09,670
[TÖREGENE]
Were those words a lie as well?

345
00:18:10,010 --> 00:18:13,260
No. I feel certain
that he truly meant them.

346
00:18:13,850 --> 00:18:14,890
Which is why

347
00:18:15,260 --> 00:18:17,640
he hadn't told me about
what he was planning to do.

348
00:18:20,680 --> 00:18:23,650
Except... I'm afraid
Chieftain Dayir

349
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:25,230
made a grave oversight.

350
00:18:25,900 --> 00:18:27,230
After everything else,

351
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:30,400
he failed to see
just how much...

352
00:18:31,030 --> 00:18:32,110
I loved him.

353
00:18:32,240 --> 00:18:34,030
[Töregene panting]

354
00:18:42,540 --> 00:18:43,920
[gasps]

355
00:18:44,630 --> 00:18:46,540
[ÖGEDEI] Oh, that's right.

356
00:18:47,550 --> 00:18:51,670
The soul of a kam
can rise up to the heavens.

357
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:55,970
And by puncturing his body,
I only helped it escape.

358
00:18:57,180 --> 00:18:59,430
A red river in the sky.

359
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:00,520
Uh?

360
00:19:00,810 --> 00:19:02,140
♪

361
00:19:04,690 --> 00:19:06,230
[ÖGEDEI] Who are you?

362
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:07,900
Uh?

363
00:19:08,020 --> 00:19:09,070
[chuckles]

364
00:19:10,990 --> 00:19:13,700
[ILÜGE] Hold on.
What are you doing here?

365
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:17,030
[TÖREGENE] Their rebellion
was put down all too easily.

366
00:19:18,120 --> 00:19:20,910
I later discovered
that they'd killed Qultuqan,

367
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:22,700
and the others as well.

368
00:19:24,750 --> 00:19:27,090
Upon Genghis Khan's
return from battle,

369
00:19:27,710 --> 00:19:30,590
Khulan learned
of the uprising they attempted.

370
00:19:31,550 --> 00:19:33,840
And the moment
she heard the news...

371
00:19:33,970 --> 00:19:34,930
Uh?

372
00:19:36,890 --> 00:19:40,390
My father brought his fate
upon himself with such folly.

373
00:19:40,510 --> 00:19:44,600
The majesty of the Khan
is something nobody can tarnish.

374
00:19:44,730 --> 00:19:45,730
[Töregene gasps]

375
00:19:46,100 --> 00:19:47,400
[TÖREGENE] Khulan...

376
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:50,650
How could you say those
awful things wearing a smile?

377
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:52,150
After that,

378
00:19:52,400 --> 00:19:56,070
I was made Ögedei's wife
and allowed to live.

379
00:19:58,620 --> 00:20:00,120
[infant crying]

380
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:03,620
[TÖREGENE] I gave birth
to his children as well.

381
00:20:04,330 --> 00:20:06,790
And the days passed by
rather peacefully.

382
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:10,420
Yet all this time,
I've been waiting...

383
00:20:11,050 --> 00:20:14,300
Secretly hoping
for a raging storm to descend,

384
00:20:14,420 --> 00:20:16,550
and ravage this empire.

385
00:20:17,050 --> 00:20:18,640
I saved you earlier

386
00:20:18,760 --> 00:20:20,760
because your smile
seemed familiar.

387
00:20:21,260 --> 00:20:24,220
From that first day,
I saw Khulan in you.

388
00:20:24,470 --> 00:20:26,390
After all these years,

389
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:29,810
I know how sad and powerless
she must have felt inside.

390
00:20:30,650 --> 00:20:31,730
But still...

391
00:20:32,230 --> 00:20:34,780
she understood what she needed
to do and fulfilled her role.

392
00:20:35,190 --> 00:20:37,400
Back then, I should've known

393
00:20:37,530 --> 00:20:39,620
how she was actually feeling,
and yet...

394
00:20:39,740 --> 00:20:41,080
[Sitara breathes uneasily]

395
00:20:41,910 --> 00:20:43,160
-So tell me...
-[gasps]

396
00:20:43,490 --> 00:20:45,080
...who are you really?

397
00:20:45,370 --> 00:20:47,580
[stutters] I'm, uh...

398
00:20:48,460 --> 00:20:49,750
That's all right.

399
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:51,920
Regardless of who you may be,
you still can't--

400
00:20:52,050 --> 00:20:53,630
I spoke
to Princess Sorghaghtani.

401
00:20:54,590 --> 00:20:56,420
According to what she said,

402
00:20:56,550 --> 00:21:00,470
there is an imbalance of power
between Tolui and the Kha'an.

403
00:21:00,590 --> 00:21:01,890
In other words,

404
00:21:02,010 --> 00:21:04,470
the empire has never been
weaker than it is right now.

405
00:21:04,600 --> 00:21:06,430
Then you must be...

406
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:11,150
My name is Sitara. I am a slave.

407
00:21:11,610 --> 00:21:13,230
The Mongol army
attacked our city

408
00:21:13,360 --> 00:21:14,610
and killed my mistress,

409
00:21:14,730 --> 00:21:17,030
then stole a book
that was precious to her.

410
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:19,820
To honor her memory,
my final duty should have been

411
00:21:19,950 --> 00:21:21,820
getting her book back,
and yet...

412
00:21:21,950 --> 00:21:25,660
The thought that resistance
could cause further tragedy...

413
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:27,870
That is my fear.

414
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:30,880
And it's caused me
to lead a life without purpose.

415
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:34,210
But this must be the moment
I've been waiting for.

416
00:21:34,340 --> 00:21:36,050
[gasps] How so?

417
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:38,510
What could we hope
to accomplish?

418
00:21:38,630 --> 00:21:40,010
♪

419
00:21:44,890 --> 00:21:46,930
I have great knowledge.

420
00:21:47,560 --> 00:21:48,640
If you'll allow,

421
00:21:48,890 --> 00:21:51,190
I'll serve you as your
new Jada stone, Highness.

422
00:21:52,310 --> 00:21:55,320
Please, just lend me your power.

423
00:21:57,070 --> 00:22:00,700
And the two of us can summon
a fierce storm.

424
00:22:02,990 --> 00:22:05,030
[♪ closing theme song playing]

425
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:35,540
[SITARA (ADULT)]
Next time, "Brothers."

